{"content":[{"c":["ABIAH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. KJV translation for Abijah, Samuel’s son, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.8.2","r":"1Sam.8.2","rawR":"1Sam.8.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.8.2","value":"1Sam.8.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Samuel 8:2"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.28","r":"1Chr.6.28","rawR":"1Chr.6.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.28","value":"1Chr.6.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:28"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Abijah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Abijah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Abijah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Abijah #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. KJV translation of a Hebrew word in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.24","r":"1Chr.2.24","rawR":"1Chr.2.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.24","value":"1Chr.2.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 2:24"},", which renders it as a proper name referring to the wife of Hezron. Most modern translations render it “his father”: “Caleb went in to Ephrathah, the wife of Hezron his father” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). The Hebrew is difficult, with different textual families evidently preserving variant readings and thus accounting for the divergences between the versions."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. KJV translation for Abijah, Becher’s son, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.8","r":"1Chr.7.8","rawR":"1Chr.7.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.8","value":"1Chr.7.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 7:8"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Abijah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Abijah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Abijah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Abijah #5"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Samuel